---
description: Git conventions for TalentGraph (commit messages, branches, pull requests)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the conventions described in CONTRIBUTING.md.

Commit messages:
- Format: `type(scope): short description`
- Types: feat, fix, chore, docs, refactor, test, ci
- Scope: the project module (m0 to m8, or v2), omitted for cross-cutting changes
- English, imperative present ("add", not "added"), lowercase, no final period, 72 characters maximum
- One commit = one logical change; never mix unrelated changes in one message

Branches: `feature/<module>-<topic>` created from `develop`; never commit to `main`.

Never stage or commit `.env` or any file containing secrets.

When suggesting a commit message, explain in one sentence why this type and scope were chosen.
